diff --git a/docs/GRADES_SETUP_NOTES.md b/docs/GRADES_SETUP_NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..597f38c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/GRADES_SETUP_NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Grades setup notes (Patch A of the Grades pass)
+
+Setup only: **grading scales** and **assessment schemes**, per level. Mark sheets and the workflow come in the next patch. The old grades module (enter, update, publish, `my-children`) is still switched off and untouched; it is replaced in the next patch. See `GRADES_MODULE_AUDIT.md` for why.
+
+## Levels
+`default`, `primary`, `jss`, `ss`. A level with no scale or scheme of its own uses the default. `Class.level` is free text today; `levelOfClass()` maps it (Primary, Nursery, KG, Basic = primary; JSS, Junior = jss; SSS, SS, Senior = ss; anything else = default). The mark-sheet patch uses it to pick the scale and scheme for a class.
+
+## Grading scale
+A list of bands `{ minScore, grade, remark, isPass }`. **A band starts at its `minScore` and runs up to the next band's start; the top band reaches 100.** So 74.5 is in the band that starts at 70 (the old inclusive min/max bands turned 74.5 into F9). Rules: 1 to 15 bands, starts are from 0 to below 100 with at most 2 decimals, one band starts at 0, no repeated start or grade, at least one pass, and once a band is a pass every higher band is a pass. Saved in ONE transaction (the old way deleted the bands first, then created them one by one).
+Every school gets the standard scale (A1 to F9, F9 below 40 is the only fail) as its default.
+
+## Assessment scheme
+The parts a subject score is made of, in order: `{ name, kind: ca | exam, maxScore }`. **Their maximum scores add up to 100**, so every scale works on 0 to 100. 1 to 8 parts, unique names, each above 0 and at most 100 with at most 2 decimals. Default for every school: **CA 40 + Exam 60**. A school can set, for example, CA1 10 + CA2 10 + Assignment 20 + Exam 60.
+
+## Endpoints (`/grades`)
+| Route | Permission |
+|---|---|
+| GET `/grades/scales`, GET `/grades/schemes` | `grades.view` |
+| PUT `/grades/scales/:level` `{ bands }` | `grades.config` **and the plan feature `grading.custom`** |
+| PUT `/grades/schemes/:level` `{ components }` | `grades.config` (no plan feature: every school may set its split) |
+| DELETE `/grades/scales/:level`, DELETE `/grades/schemes/:level` | `grades.config` (puts the level back on the default; the default cannot be removed) |
+
+Reads return every level with `usesDefault` and the scale or scheme it really uses. Band rows carry `upTo` (the next band's start, null for the top). Changes are audited old to new (`grades.scale_updated`, `grades.scale_removed`, `grades.scheme_updated`, `grades.scheme_removed`).
+Error codes: `GRADES_LEVEL_INVALID`, `GRADES_SCALE_INVALID` and `GRADES_SCHEME_INVALID` (both list `details.problems` in plain words), `GRADES_DEFAULT_REQUIRED`.
+
+## Permissions
+`grades.view` (ALL, BRANCH, ASSIGNED, OWN) and `grades.config` (ALL, STAFF). Default roles: principal view ALL, teacher view ASSIGNED, student and guardian view OWN, school admin everything. The scope only starts to matter with results (next patch).
+
+## Migration `20261103090000_grades_setup`
+Creates `GradingScale`, `GradingBand`, `AssessmentScheme`, `AssessmentComponent` and the `AssessmentKind` type. One scale and one scheme per level, enforced by the database (unique index on the level, empty counted as the default). The default scale is **copied from the school's existing `GradingConfig` list when that list is usable** (it must start at 0 with no repeated starting score; a band is a pass from 40 up). An empty list (every new school) or an unusable one gets the standard scale, and a notice is printed for the unusable case. The default scheme is CA 40 + Exam 60. Nothing is deleted: `GradingConfig` stays until the next patch replaces the old module.
+
+**Deploy order:** `git pull`, `git apply grades-setup.patch`, `npm run prisma:generate`, `npm run migrate:apply-to-existing-schools:dry-run`, `npm run migrate:apply-to-existing-schools`, `npm run sync:registries`, `npm run sync:school-roles:dry-run`, `npm run sync:school-roles`. (The last two give existing schools' roles `grades.view`.)
+
+## Frontend
+New: the six routes above. The old `/grades/config` routes were never switched on and are not replaced one-for-one: use `/grades/scales` and `/grades/schemes`.
+
+## Tests (`tests/grades/`, 22)
+`grades.policy.test.ts` (level mapping, 74.5, every band and scheme rule, request shapes, permissions), `grades-setup.db.test.ts` (real Postgres: defaults in a new school, saving and removing per level, invalid input changes nothing, all-or-nothing replace, audit old to new, database rules), `migration.db.test.ts` (populated schools: usable list copied, empty and unusable lists replaced). Database tests need `TEST_DATABASE_URL`.
+**Not run:** HTTP calls to the routes (the app was not started) and the plan-feature gate on `PUT /grades/scales/:level` (it uses the same `requireFeature` as the fees routes).
+
+## Next
+Patch B: mark sheets and the workflow (draft, submitted, approved, published, locked), scores per part, positions with ties, parents and students see published sheets only.
diff --git a/prisma/tenant-migrations/20261103090000_grades_setup/migration.sql b/prisma/tenant-migrations/20261103090000_grades_setup/migration.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..55206be
--- /dev/null
+++ b/prisma/tenant-migrations/20261103090000_grades_setup/migration.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+-- Grades setup: grading scales and assessment schemes per level (level empty = the default for all levels).
+
+CREATE TYPE "AssessmentKind" AS ENUM ('ca', 'exam');
+
+CREATE TABLE "GradingScale" (
+    "id" TEXT NOT NULL, "name" TEXT NOT NULL, "level" TEXT,
+    "createdAt" TIMESTAMP(3) NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, "updatedAt" TIMESTAMP(3) NOT NULL,
+    CONSTRAINT "GradingScale_pkey" PRIMARY KEY ("id")
+);
+CREATE TABLE "GradingBand" (
+    "id" TEXT NOT NULL, "scaleId" TEXT NOT NULL, "minScore" DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL,
+    "grade" TEXT NOT NULL, "remark" TEXT NOT NULL, "isPass" BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
+    "createdAt" TIMESTAMP(3) NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
+    CONSTRAINT "GradingBand_pkey" PRIMARY KEY ("id")
+);
+CREATE TABLE "AssessmentScheme" (
+    "id" TEXT NOT NULL, "name" TEXT NOT NULL, "level" TEXT,
+    "createdAt" TIMESTAMP(3) NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, "updatedAt" TIMESTAMP(3) NOT NULL,
+    CONSTRAINT "AssessmentScheme_pkey" PRIMARY KEY ("id")
+);
+CREATE TABLE "AssessmentComponent" (
+    "id" TEXT NOT NULL, "schemeId" TEXT NOT NULL, "name" TEXT NOT NULL, "kind" "AssessmentKind" NOT NULL,
+    "maxScore" DOUBLE PRECISION NOT NULL, "position" INTEGER NOT NULL,
+    "createdAt" TIMESTAMP(3) NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
+    CONSTRAINT "AssessmentComponent_pkey" PRIMARY KEY ("id")
+);
+
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "GradingBand_scaleId_minScore_key" ON "GradingBand"("scaleId", "minScore");
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "AssessmentComponent_schemeId_position_key" ON "AssessmentComponent"("schemeId", "position");
+-- one scale and one scheme per level (an empty level is the default); Prisma cannot declare these, so they live only here
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "GradingScale_level_key" ON "GradingScale"(COALESCE("level", '__default'));
+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX "AssessmentScheme_level_key" ON "AssessmentScheme"(COALESCE("level", '__default'));
+ALTER TABLE "GradingBand" ADD CONSTRAINT "GradingBand_scaleId_fkey" FOREIGN KEY ("scaleId") REFERENCES "GradingScale"("id") ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE;
+ALTER TABLE "AssessmentComponent" ADD CONSTRAINT "AssessmentComponent_schemeId_fkey" FOREIGN KEY ("schemeId") REFERENCES "AssessmentScheme"("id") ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE;
+ALTER TABLE "GradingBand" ADD CONSTRAINT "GradingBand_minScore_check" CHECK ("minScore" >= 0 AND "minScore" < 100);
+ALTER TABLE "AssessmentComponent" ADD CONSTRAINT "AssessmentComponent_maxScore_check" CHECK ("maxScore" > 0 AND "maxScore" <= 100);
+
+-- The DEFAULT scale. The school's existing grading list is copied across when it is usable: it must start at 0 and have no
+-- two bands with the same starting score. Otherwise (empty, as in every new school, or unusable) the standard WAEC scale
+-- is used. A band is a pass from 40 up, matching the standard scale.
+DO $$
+DECLARE
+    scale_id TEXT := gen_random_uuid()::text;
+    usable   BOOLEAN;
+BEGIN
+    INSERT INTO "GradingScale"("id", "name", "level", "updatedAt") VALUES (scale_id, 'Default', NULL, now());
+
+    SELECT (count(*) > 0 AND min("minScore") = 0 AND count(*) = count(DISTINCT "minScore") AND min("minScore") >= 0 AND max("minScore") < 100)
+      INTO usable FROM "GradingConfig";
+
+    IF usable THEN
+        INSERT INTO "GradingBand"("id", "scaleId", "minScore", "grade", "remark", "isPass")
+        SELECT gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, "minScore", "grade", "remark", "minScore" >= 40 FROM "GradingConfig";
+    ELSE
+        IF (SELECT count(*) FROM "GradingConfig") > 0 THEN
+            RAISE NOTICE 'The existing grading list could not be used (it must start at 0 with no repeated starting scores): the standard A1 to F9 scale was used instead.';
+        END IF;
+        INSERT INTO "GradingBand"("id", "scaleId", "minScore", "grade", "remark", "isPass") VALUES
+            (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 75, 'A1', 'Excellent', true), (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 70, 'B2', 'Very Good', true),
+            (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 65, 'B3', 'Good', true),      (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 60, 'C4', 'Credit', true),
+            (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 55, 'C5', 'Credit', true),    (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 50, 'C6', 'Credit', true),
+            (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 45, 'D7', 'Pass', true),      (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 40, 'E8', 'Pass', true),
+            (gen_random_uuid()::text, scale_id, 0,  'F9', 'Fail', false);
+    END IF;
+END $$;
+
+-- The DEFAULT scheme: continuous assessment 40 + exam 60
+DO $$
+DECLARE scheme_id TEXT := gen_random_uuid()::text;
+BEGIN
+    INSERT INTO "AssessmentScheme"("id", "name", "level", "updatedAt") VALUES (scheme_id, 'Default', NULL, now());
+    INSERT INTO "AssessmentComponent"("id", "schemeId", "name", "kind", "maxScore", "position") VALUES
+        (gen_random_uuid()::text, scheme_id, 'CA', 'ca', 40, 1), (gen_random_uuid()::text, scheme_id, 'Exam', 'exam', 60, 2);
+END $$;
diff --git a/prisma/tenant.prisma b/prisma/tenant.prisma
index f0fe6d6..56faa84 100644
--- a/prisma/tenant.prisma
+++ b/prisma/tenant.prisma
@@ -2149,3 +2149,59 @@ model SalaryTransfer {
   @@index([runId])
   @@index([status])
 }
+
+// ── Grades setup: grading scales and assessment schemes, one per level (level empty = the default for all levels) ──
+enum AssessmentKind {
+  ca
+  exam
+}
+
+model GradingScale {
+  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
+  name      String
+  level     String?  // primary | jss | ss, or empty for the default. One scale per level (SQL unique index)
+  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
+  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
+
+  bands GradingBand[]
+}
+
+// A band starts at minScore and runs up to the next band's minScore (the top band reaches 100)
+model GradingBand {
+  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
+  scaleId   String
+  minScore  Float
+  grade     String
+  remark    String
+  isPass    Boolean  @default(true)
+  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
+
+  scale GradingScale @relation(fields: [scaleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
+
+  @@unique([scaleId, minScore])
+}
+
+model AssessmentScheme {
+  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
+  name      String
+  level     String?  // primary | jss | ss, or empty for the default. One scheme per level (SQL unique index)
+  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
+  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
+
+  components AssessmentComponent[]
+}
+
+// The maximum scores of one scheme's components add up to 100
+model AssessmentComponent {
+  id        String         @id @default(uuid())
+  schemeId  String
+  name      String
+  kind      AssessmentKind
+  maxScore  Float
+  position  Int
+  createdAt DateTime       @default(now())
+
+  scheme AssessmentScheme @relation(fields: [schemeId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
+
+  @@unique([schemeId, position])
+}
